    },
    {
      "text": "Place egg yolks and lemon juice in a blender to create hollandaise sauce. Blend the mixture until it becomes a pale yellow.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bacon-and-eggs-benedict-salad/#wprm-recipe-52846-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/bacon-and-egg-benedict-salad-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt the butter in a microwave-safe dish until it begins to bubble. Drizzle melted butter into blender mixture and blend until the sauce is well combined. It will be light in color and will thicken as it begins to cool.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bacon-and-eggs-benedict-salad/#wprm-recipe-52846-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/bacon-and-egg-benedict-salad-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place greens, sliced tomatoes, and bacon slices on a plate to form a salad bed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bacon-and-eggs-benedict-salad/#wprm-recipe-52846-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/bacon-and-egg-benedict-salad-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Apply a layer of parmesan cheese to the salad bed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bacon-and-eggs-benedict-salad/#wprm-recipe-52846-step-0-5",
